# ============================================================================
# File:     FleetManagement/.gitignore
# Purpose:  Root-level Git ignore rules preventing tool artifacts, secrets,
#           and platform-specific build outputs from ever being tracked in
#           the FleetManagement monorepo.
#
# Why it exists:
#   The Frozen Stack (Fleet-Management-Stack.pdf) mandates a polyglot
#   monorepo with pnpm workspaces + Turborepo, Expo driver-app, Next.js
#   ops-web, NestJS api, BullMQ worker, and Terraform IaC. Each of those
#   tools produces build artifacts, caches, or state files that must not
#   enter version control — and critically, secret material (.env*,
#   Terraform state, signing keys) must be blocked at the source. This
#   file is the first line of defense; the pre-commit hooks in
#   .pre-commit-config.yaml are the second.
#
# Key decisions / invariants:
#   - .env* is blocked globally with an allowlist exception for .env.example
#     (template files that MUST be committed so new contributors can scaffold
#     their local env).
#   - Terraform state (*.tfstate, *.tfvars) is blocked because it contains
#     plaintext DB passwords, S3 credentials, and IdP secrets. Only
#     *.tfvars.example is allowed.
#   - Expo native build directories (apps/driver-app/ios, android) and
#     signing materials (*.jks, *.p8, *.p12, *.mobileprovision) are blocked
#     — these are regenerated by EAS Build and must never be committed.
#   - .turbo/ is the local Turborepo cache; always machine-specific.
#   - .pnpm-store/ is pnpm's content-addressed store.
#   - .vscode/* blocked with explicit allowlist for settings.json and
#     extensions.json (shared team editor setup).
#   - Keeps !negation patterns close to their block patterns for readability.
#
# Related files:
#   - .pre-commit-config.yaml  — hooks that re-enforce these bans at commit
#   - SECURITY.md              — rationale for secret-blocking policy
#   - .github/workflows/ci.yml — CI uses pnpm cache paths these rules cover
# ============================================================================

# Node / pnpm
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.pnpm-debug.log*
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Build outputs
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
.turbo/
.expo/
.expo-shared/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Logs / coverage / test artifacts
logs/
*.log
coverage/
.nyc_output/
junit.xml
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Terraform
infra/terraform/.terraform/
infra/terraform/*.tfstate
infra/terraform/*.tfstate.*
infra/terraform/*.tfvars
!infra/terraform/*.tfvars.example
infra/terraform/.terraform.lock.hcl.backup

# Expo / native
apps/driver-app/ios/
apps/driver-app/android/
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision

# Misc
*.tgz
.cache/
packages/*/reports/
packages/*/.stryker-tmp/
/playwright/.cache/

# Stryker mutation-testing temporary artifacts (large; never commit)
.stryker-tmp/
**/.stryker-tmp/

# Stryker mutation testing artifacts
reports/

# curl debugging artifacts
cookies.txt

# E2E runtime handoff artifacts (driver-leg credentials emitted by dispatcher-to-driver spec)
.e2e-artifacts/

# TS incremental + Vite optimizer caches (stale-replay hygiene)
.vite/
